  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_037 (scvi_n200, ViT-L, avgpool, weighted) at 0.706 acc. All multimodal experiments so far have used avgpool aggregation; transformer aggregation has only been tested in RNA-only settings where it underperformed avgpool by ~7 points (0.519 vs 0.591). However, in the multimodal context with a strong ViT-L image encoder, transformer aggregation might capture cross-profile interactions that avgpool averages away, potentially complementing the image signal differently. Question: Does transformer aggregation improve upon avgpool in the multimodal+ViT-L+scvi_n200+weighted setting? Why this experiment: It is the single most informative next step because (1) it is a minimal, controlled change from the current best (only aggregation differs), isolating the effect of one design variable; (2) if it improves, it identifies a new promising direction; if it does not, it definitively rules out transformer aggregation for the top-performing family, saving future budget from exploring dead ends; (3) under a limited budget, confirming or refuting the best aggregation strategy at the highest-performing operating point maximizes information per experiment."
}

